<notes>
- V7: a warehouse entry violates when `max_units > capacity`. The measured value is the list of `wh` names for violating entries, in input order. The same warehouse can appear more than once if it appears in several runs.
- V8: I read "all expiries were notified" as per-run. An expiry in one entry is only satisfied by a notification in the same entry. It is matched on the full `[sku, wh, qty]` triple, so a quantity mismatch counts as unnotified. The measured value is a list of unmatched `(sku, wh, qty)` tuples. If the spec means matching on `(sku, wh)` only, or matching across runs, this needs changing.
- V9: the reliability range is an assumption (0..100 inclusive), held in `RELIABILITY_MIN`/`RELIABILITY_MAX`. I've asked the owner to confirm it. The measured value is the list of out-of-range supplier names.
- V7–V9 have no clause IDs in the spec, so their docstrings use only the validator name, unlike V1–V2 and V4 in `validators.py`.
- Tests use stdlib `unittest` and are in `tests/test_validators_later.py`, which assumes `validators_later.py` is importable from the repo root. I did not run them.
- `validators.py` is unchanged.
</notes>
